## Install OpenHPC Base Packages

Now OpenHPC packages can be installed. The `ohpc-base` meta-package requires a
module tool to manage the user environment, and OpenHPC provides two of them:
[Lmod](https://lmod.readthedocs.io) in the `lmod-ohpc` package and
[Environment Modules](https://modules.readthedocs.io) in the
`environment-modules-ohpc` package. Both read the OpenHPC module hierarchy and
provide the `module` command. The `${modules_package}` variable in `input.local`
selects the one installed on the head node and, later in this guide, on the
compute nodes; it defaults to `lmod-ohpc`. To add the base package and the
module tool on the head node issue the following:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Install OpenHPC base packages and the module tool -->
```bash
{{ pkg_install }} ohpc-base ${modules_package:-lmod-ohpc}
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

::: {.tip}
Naming the module tool keeps the choice explicit; `ohpc-base` alone normally
pulls in Lmod, which it suggests. The two tools can also be installed side by
side: the startup scripts `/etc/profile.d/modules.sh` and `modules.csh`, which
define the `module` command, and `/usr/bin/modulecmd` are links managed with
`alternatives`, and `environment-modules-ohpc` takes precedence over `lmod-ohpc`
when both are present. Run `alternatives --config modules.sh` to select the
active tool.
:::
